      "nets": ["+3V3", "Net-(U1-B)"],
      "observed": "R8 is specified with value \"2.2\" (ohms) in the netlist, connected between +3V3 and the MAX3485 B line (Net-(U1-B)).",
      "expected": "R8 should be 2.2k (2200 ohms) as stated in the design specification's bias/pull network for the MAX3485 A/B lines.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R8\") (value \"2.2\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric\") ... (field (name \"LCSC\") \"C4190\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R6, R7, R8, R15 | 2k, 20k, 2.2k, 2.2k | Bias/pull network on the MAX3485 A/B differential lines and DE/RE enable line."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If R8 is populated as 2.2Ω instead of 2.2kΩ, it will strongly pull the RS-485 B line to +3V3, disrupting the intended bias network and likely preventing reliable serial servo communication. The LCSC field C4190 indicates the intended part is 2.2kΩ, but the value field is incorrect.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one anomaly: R8's value is listed as 2.2 (ohms) instead of the specified 2.2k, which would corrupt the MAX3485 bias network if populated as written."
}

